 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 282405,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Explain the error in the following calculation. Determine the correct answer:\n<span data-math=\"{49_{14}} \\times {9_{14}} = {441_{14}}\">{49_{14}} \\times {9_{14}} = {441_{14}}</span>",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "This is correct if the numbers are base 10 numbers, but these numbers are base 14 numbers. In base 14, <span data-math=\"{49_{14}} \\times {9_{14}} = 2{\\text{D}}{{\\text{B}}_{14}}\">{49_{14}} \\times {9_{14}} = 2{\\text{D}}{{\\text{B}}_{14}}</span> is not 81, but instead is 5B. Careful use of the base 14 addition table (Table 4.9) generates the correct answer, <span data-math=\"{49_{14}} \\times {9_{14}} = 2{\\text{D}}{{\\text{B}}_{14}}\">{49_{14}} \\times {9_{14}} = 2{\\text{D}}{{\\text{B}}_{14}}</span>."
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
